.TH HIRO 1 "August 2026" "HIRO" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hiro \- enroll and manage face templates for HIRO authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hiro
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
HIRO ("Hello, InfraRed, On Linux") provides Windows Hello-style face
authentication on Linux using the built-in IR camera. \fBhiro\fR talks to
the \fBhirod\fR(8) daemon to enroll, test, and manage encrypted face
templates.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enroll [USER] [--max N]
Capture face templates. Stand in front of the IR camera and follow the
quality feedback; frames that are blurry, too small, or duplicates are
rejected automatically, and you can hold each pose for a sharp capture
(no constant movement is required). The optional
\fBrecognition.enroll_min_variance\fR setting re-enables rejecting static
frames when enforced. With \fBrecognition.auto_threshold\fR (default on),
enrollment ends with a short calibration pass that measures your genuine
match scores and stores a per-user match threshold; the calibrated value is
printed and shown in \fBhiro test\fR output as \fBthreshold\fR. Re-enroll to
recalibrate (e.g. after changing camera, lighting, or appearance).
.TP
.B test
Run a verification attempt against your own templates. Prints the best
score seen and the effective threshold even on a miss, so you can see how
close an attempt came and how the per-user threshold is moving.
.TP
.B list [USER]
List enrolled templates.
.TP
.B remove USER --id N
Remove one template.
.TP
.B clear [USER]
Remove all templates.
.TP
.B keyring set [USER]
Seal the login password so face login unlocks the keyring (GNOME Keyring /
KWallet). You are prompted twice to guard against typos; the password is
verified against the account, then stored encrypted under the TPM-sealed
data key. Re-run after changing your login password.
.TP
.B keyring clear [USER]
Drop the sealed keyring password.
.TP
.B keyring status [USER]
Show whether keyring unlock is enabled and a password is stored.
.TP
.B doctor
Run hardware diagnostics: camera discovery, IR detection, emitter support,
model integrity, and daemon reachability.
.TP
.B status
Show daemon status.
.TP
.B ping
Check daemon reachability.
.TP
.B prewarm
Ask the daemon to warm the camera and models.
.TP
.B reload
Reload the daemon configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --socket PATH
Daemon socket path (default \fI/run/hirod/hirod.sock\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hirod (8),
.BR pam_hiro (8),
.BR hiro.conf (5)
